1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,927
This is a website template for a fertility clinic, shown with placeholder details.

2
00:00:05,927 --> 00:00:09,389
Let's see what each part does for patients, and for the clinic.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,500
The site opens with Life Unfolds: the IVF journey, told as visitors scroll.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,791
The story isn't a video: the visitor's browser draws each frame live, in 3D.

5
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,155
Patients can compare conventional IVF with ICSI,

6
00:00:46,155 --> 00:00:49,775
where one sperm is injected into each mature egg.

7
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:05,892
The transfer takes the real path, through the cervix,

8
00:01:05,892 --> 00:01:08,520
with the embryo labelled as enlarged.

9
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,675
The baby's size follows typical growth.

10
00:01:22,675 --> 00:01:26,779
Every scene is marked as an illustration, not a patient's result.

11
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:39,884
Below the story, the home page introduces the clinic.

12
00:01:39,884 --> 00:01:44,733
In review mode, dashed tags flag sample text and content awaiting approval.

13
00:01:44,733 --> 00:01:46,446
Next come four commitments.

14
00:01:46,446 --> 00:01:51,967
By design, the site shows no success rates: outcomes are discussed with each person.

15
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:55,185
Then patients meet the doctor who leads the clinic's care.

16
00:01:55,185 --> 00:01:59,631
Here it's a sample profile, with a line drawing in place of a photograph.

17
00:01:59,633 --> 00:02:02,243
An index covers all fourteen treatments.

18
00:02:02,243 --> 00:02:05,844
When the mouse passes over one, a small lens shows its drawing.

19
00:02:05,844 --> 00:02:09,267
Those the clinic doesn't offer are removed before launch.

20
00:02:09,267 --> 00:02:14,241
In the laboratory section, five images from the same 3D engine glide past,

21
00:02:14,241 --> 00:02:16,779
each labelled as a visualisation.

22
00:02:16,779 --> 00:02:21,367
Claims that need proof, like the clean room, stay flagged until documented.

23
00:02:21,367 --> 00:02:24,498
Testimonials change only when the visitor clicks.

24
00:02:24,498 --> 00:02:26,295
In this demo, they're samples,

25
00:02:26,295 --> 00:02:30,351
and a note explains that reviews describe care, not outcomes.

26
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:33,224
Common questions get short, plain answers.

27
00:02:33,224 --> 00:02:37,553
Asked whether IVF can guarantee a pregnancy, the site says no.

28
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:42,649
At the bottom, a short form lets visitors ask for a call, without leaving the page.

29
00:02:44,933 --> 00:02:48,242
Hovering over Treatments opens the full list, in groups.

30
00:02:48,242 --> 00:02:52,474
The menu and the pages are built from one file, so they always match.

31
00:02:53,533 --> 00:02:58,483
Each treatment has a page like this, tagged for review by the clinic's medical team.

32
00:02:58,483 --> 00:03:03,191
All fourteen are laid out in six parts, including risks and limitations.

33
00:03:05,067 --> 00:03:06,188
Before a first visit,

34
00:03:06,188 --> 00:03:10,192
patients can get to know the Medical Director through a full profile.

35
00:03:10,192 --> 00:03:13,544
It's set in one file, ready for the clinic's own doctor.

36
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:19,395
Room by room, the Facilities page describes each space.

37
00:03:19,395 --> 00:03:23,376
Instead of borrowed photographs, 3D images show the work done there,

38
00:03:23,376 --> 00:03:26,352
and dashed frames wait for the clinic's own.

39
00:03:28,533 --> 00:03:32,549
The Patient stories page labels each testimonial as a sample.

40
00:03:32,549 --> 00:03:35,633
Real ones need written permission and a legal check,

41
00:03:35,633 --> 00:03:39,057
since medical advertising rules may not allow them.

42
00:03:40,933 --> 00:03:42,171
In the knowledge centre,

43
00:03:42,171 --> 00:03:46,462
eight plain-language guides help patients prepare questions for their doctor.

44
00:03:46,462 --> 00:03:50,771
Search looks through the full text as you type, and topics narrow the list.

45
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:55,504
Each article waits for a clinician's check,

46
00:03:55,504 --> 00:04:00,479
and ends by saying it's general education, not personal medical advice.

47
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:05,605
On the contact page, the request reads as one sentence,

48
00:04:05,605 --> 00:04:10,385
the way a person would say it: a name, a phone number and a preferred date.

49
00:04:10,385 --> 00:04:12,376
A checkbox asks for consent.

50
00:04:14,933 --> 00:04:18,804
The thank-you appears only once the request has been forwarded,

51
00:04:18,804 --> 00:04:21,765
by email or to a system the clinic chooses.

52
00:04:21,765 --> 00:04:24,400
This one went to a test server, not a clinic.

53
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:27,011
The footer says plainly that this is a demo.

54
00:04:27,011 --> 00:04:30,306
A link there opens the launch checklist: sixty items,

55
00:04:30,306 --> 00:04:35,492
from phone numbers to medical and legal review, most with the file to change.

56
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:42,396
On phones, the same 3D story runs, adapting its quality to each device.

57
00:04:42,396 --> 00:04:48,069
Where 3D can't run, or a visitor prefers less motion, there's a still version instead.

58
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:54,123
The full-screen menu keeps treatments grouped.

59
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,887
Before launch, placeholders are replaced,

60
00:04:57,887 --> 00:05:02,224
medical content is approved, and requests are directed to the clinic.

61
00:05:02,224 --> 00:05:06,997
Then demo and review modes are switched off, and the site becomes the clinic's own.
